---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is Cleanroom a fork of Forge?', a: 'It started as one. Since then most of the work has moved out of Forge’s code: Cleanroom still includes Forge, keeps fixing its performance and bugs, and has grown into its own ecosystem with new APIs and frameworks.' },
  { q: 'Will my Forge mods work?', a: 'Almost all of them, about 99%. A few known problem mods need removing or swapping first: the Preparing your modpack guide lists them.' },
  { q: 'Which Java do I need?', a: 'Java 25 or newer. The Cleanroom Relauncher can download a compatible Java for you.' },
  { q: 'Which launchers are supported?', a: 'MultiMC-based launchers (Prism, MultiMC) can import the instance zip. The official Minecraft Launcher uses the installer jar. On any other launcher, add the Cleanroom Relauncher mod to a Forge instance.' },
  { q: 'Can I run it on a server?', a: 'Yes. Use the installer jar to set up a dedicated server, and follow the Server guide in the wiki.' },
];
---

<section class="ls ls-faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <p class="ls-eyebrow">FAQ</p>
  <h2 class="ls-h" id="faq-h">Questions people ask first.</h2>
  <div class="ls-faq__list">
    {
      faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <details class="ls-q" open={i === 0}>
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <p>{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="ls-faq__more">More in the <a href="/wiki/end-user-guide/introduction/">End User Guide</a> and <a href="/wiki/end-user-guide/preparing-your-modpack/">Preparing your modpack</a>.</p>
</section>
